    "content" : "WHAT MAKES THE ROOSEVELT COMMUNITY CENTER GREEN?"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H3",
    "id" : 11,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 388.0, 553.78, 513.19, 569.432 ],
    "heading level" : 3,
    "font" : "NeutraText-Bold",
    "font size" : 13.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "BUILDING PROFILE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 388.0, 494.696, 564.653, 553.887 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Located in Roosevelt Park east of downtown San José, the Roosevelt Community Center offers a wide range of recreational and educational programs for all ages, making it a cornerstone of the neighborhood."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.818, 454.078, 67.198, 482.248 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "1529b213d5db3acb5254d34f81d18e060f28_pg1_images/imageFile2.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 73.0, 424.644, 305.826, 484.006 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "BUILDING LOCATION & COMMUNITY IMPACTBuilt on a former industrial site, the Center acts as a gateway between Roosevelt Park and Santa Clara Street, a neighborhood business district and VTA Bus Rapid Transit corridor. It is accessible via public transit and bicycle."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.818, 371.987, 67.198, 400.157 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "1529b213d5db3acb5254d34f81d18e060f28_pg1_images/imageFile3.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 73.0, 357.164, 327.524, 404.526 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "WATER EFFICIENCY—Rainwater is collected and filtered onsite through planted basins, then used to irrigate landscaped areas. Metered faucets and low-flow toilets reduce indoor water consumption by 34 percent as compared to a standard building."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 27,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.818, 307.828, 67.198, 335.998 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "1529b213d5db3acb5254d34f81d18e060f28_pg1_images/imageFile4.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 73.0, 289.684, 326.327, 337.046 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "ENERGY & EMISSIONS—Natural light and motion sensors reduce the need for electric lighting. A highly insulated roof and exterior walls help make the building 44 percent more energy efficient than required by the State Building Code."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.818, 241.078, 67.198, 269.248 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "1529b213d5db3acb5254d34f81d18e060f28_pg1_images/imageFile5.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 73.0, 198.204, 328.882, 269.566 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "MATERIALS & WASTE—More than 14 percent of building materials used for the Center include recycled content, 30 percent were manufactured within a 500-mile radius, and over 86 percent of the construction wood is FSC (Forest Stewardship Council) certified which means it came from responsibly managed forests."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 29,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.818, 148.828, 67.198, 176.998 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "1529b213d5db3acb5254d34f81d18e060f28_pg1_images/imageFile6.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 73.0, 130.724, 322.394, 178.086 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "HEALTH & SAFETY—No- and low-VOC (volatile organic compound) emitting finishes and paints were chosen for the building interior. This contributes to healthier indoor air quality for staff and visitors."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H4",
    "id" : 20,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 42.545, 79.843, 232.099, 91.281 ],
    "heading level" : 4,
    "font" : "NeutraText-Bold",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "SAN JOSE’S GREEN VISION IN ACTION"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 42.545, 13.723, 344.081, 73.211 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 8.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "LEED certification of the Roosevelt Community Center contributes to achieving the San José Green Vision goal to build or retrofit 50 million square feet of green buildings by 2022. It supports additional Green Vision goals related to energy and water efficiency, recycled water use, and waste reduction. San José policies promote green building practices to reduce the impact of the built environment on global climate change. www.sanjoseca.gov/greenvision"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 388.0, 451.216, 585.752, 486.578 ],
    "font" : "NeutraText-Book",
    "font size" : 9.5,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "FUNCTION: Multi-purpose community center, including a fitness community meeting and recreation rooms, and senior centers."
